{"author":{"id":"6af04b5756f10b3005a23338b8f25a6c1d7564fe1ddddc77e70806b2f14ac31a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788929793,"nonce":"yo9kFBOKSNExs1mgAq4HDBr1Zr0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABQZOKrQ","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/gic-lang/issues/5","origin":"github"},"title":"Dynamic Lists in lang rev 3","message":"To support dynmaic lists aka Arrays we need to do quite some work.\n\n```gic\nlet a = [];\nlet b = [1,2,3];\nlet c= [true, false, true];\nlet d = [true, 1, [1,2,3]]; // error due to mixed types? Is this possible in a dynamic language?\nlet e = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6]]; // works\nlet f = [a, b, c];\nf[4] = 2; // will this work since f has a length of 3? we get a hole?\n\n```\n\n\n\nMinimal:\n\n```ebnf\nprimary = NUMBER | STRING | \"true\" | \"false\" | IDENTIFIER | arrayLiteral | \"(\" expression \")\" ;\n\narrayLiteral = \"[\" ( expression ( \",\" expression )* )? \"]\" ;\n```\n\nAnd indexing — should I mention it? It's a natural follow-up but they asked \"how would an array fit\". Indexing needs postfix in callExpr or primary. I can offer it as optional next step, briefly.\n\nShow the change: add arrayLiteral alternative to primary. Also if they want indexing: add postfix rule. Keep short. No citations needed.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\nIt fits in `primary`, since an array literal is a primary expression:\n\n```ebnf\nprimary = NUMBER | STRING | \"true\" | \"false\" | IDENTIFIER | arrayLiteral | \"(\" expression \")\" ;\n\narrayLiteral = \"[\" ( expression ( \",\" expression )* )? \"]\" ;\n```\n\nThat's the minimal change — `varDecl`, `exprStmt`, arguments, etc. all work automatically since they go through `expression`.\n\nIf you also want **indexing** (`a[0]`, `arr[i+1]`), add it as a postfix next to `callExpr`, so it chains naturally:\n\n```ebnf\ncallExpr = IDENTIFIER \"(\" arguments? \")\" | postfix ;\npostfix  = primary ( \"[\" expression \"]\" )* ;\n```\n\nNote: as written, indexing won't work on assignment targets (`a[0] = 1` fails because `assignment` only accepts a bare `IDENTIFIER`). If you need that, extend `assignment`:\n\n```ebnf\nassignment = postfix \"=\" expression \";\" ;\n```\n\nand validate in the parser/semantic phase that the left side is a valid assignable target.","files":null}]}